{#
   THE READ-ONLY METADATA GRID — "ID #12 · Créé le 02/08/2026 10:41".

   Six `edit` pages carried their own copy, and every copy declared its own
   colours inline:

       .readonly-item  { background: #f9fafb; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; }
       .readonly-label { color: #6b7280; }
       .readonly-value { color: #111827; }

   ⚠️ **Four literal hex values, so all six were dark-mode holes** — grey on grey
   in the dark theme, which is why `machines-list.css` having zero literal colours
   is the rule the rest of the CSS is being moved towards. The rules now live in
   `admin.css` on tokens, and this partial is the only markup.

   Parameters:

     items  a list of `{label: '…', value: '…'}`, both already translated and
            already formatted. ⚠️ Formatted by the caller on purpose: `createdAt`
            is a machine timestamp and needs `|lab_date`, while a booking date is
            lab wall-clock and needs plain `|date`. A partial that formatted
            dates itself would have to guess which convention it was handed, and
            guessing wrong shifts by hours in silence.
#}
{% if items|default([])|length %}
    <div class="readonly-grid">
        {% for item in items %}
            <div class="readonly-item">
                <span class="readonly-label">{{ item.label }}</span>
                <span class="readonly-value">{{ item.value }}</span>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
